{
  "$comment": "Pins for the on-demand fallback fonts in community/fallback-fonts. scripts/import-fallback-fonts.ts reads each upstream file from a sparse clone of google/fonts at `commit`, refuses a file whose sha256 differs from the pin, pins the width axis at its default where the font has one (`pinWidth`), cuts the Latin, Greek and Cyrillic packs out of Noto Sans by script, cuts the Chinese, Japanese and Korean packs to a national character set (`charset`, defined in the script from the WHATWG encoding indexes pinned under `charsets`) plus `add`, and writes WOFF2 files, the licence texts and index.json. `scripts` are ISO 15924 codes: a pack fills characters of those scripts that a design system's fonts cannot draw. `han` is the language whose Han forms a Chinese, Japanese or Korean pack draws. `version` is the upstream font version in the catalog's three-part grammar (2.012 becomes 2.12.0).",
  "source": {
    "repository": "https://github.com/google/fonts",
    "commit": "38411257417e616c5d4daa1b9e91a3dbcebe1c2e"
  },
  "charsets": {
    "$comment": "The national character sets the Chinese, Japanese and Korean packs are cut to, read from the Encoding Standard's index files at this commit (fetched with git into dist/, never committed, each checked against its sha256). Only which code points each set holds is used. `runningText` is added to every one of those packs: the punctuation, dashes, quotation marks and fullwidth forms their running text uses.",
